A||||3||SCCA FIERO||HOLY COW!!! 
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||05-29-99||09:40 PM||||I replaced my alumunim clutch pedal with a steel unit. WOW!! I cant beleive it. It shifts as smooth as silk!!!! WOW!!! Like a new system was put in. I couldn't get my 86SE V6 4 speed into reverse without grinding the gears. Now it slips right in. I didn't relize it but the old pedal was bent bad. Now all I have to do is learn how to drive it since it engages/disengages within the first inch of travel instead of the last inch. Much Much better!!
Z||000001||87FieroGT||05-29-99||11:06 PM||||Where did you get the new clutch pedal and how much did it cost?
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||05-30-99||01:04 AM||||My fellow Fiero buddy gave it to me. The local Pontiac dealer want about $35.00 for a new steel unit. Well worth it if you have an alumunim unit! It was little tricky to install because of the ackward position. I took out my sunroof and stuck my feet out it. I think the 87 to 88 Fieros all have steel pedals but i could be wrong. Just throw a magnet on it and find out.
Z||000003||Phil||05-30-99||04:55 AM||||I've mentioned the pedal several times and what a difference it makes. Finally somebody agrees with me.
